        <body>
            <div type="edition" xml:space="preserve">
                <ab>
                    <lb n="1"/><hi rend="ligature">Ηγ</hi><hi rend="ligature">ου</hi>μενευον<hi rend="ligature">το</hi>ς
                    <lb n="2"/>οἰκ<hi rend="ligature">τρ</hi><hi rend="ligature">οῦ</hi> <persName type="attested" ref="#pers16">Μαξίμ<hi rend="ligature">ου</hi></persName>
                    <lb n="3"/>ο <expan><abbr>φ<hi rend="ligature">ού</hi>ρνο</abbr><ex>ς</ex></expan> <expan><abbr><hi rend="ligature">ου</hi><hi rend="ligature">το</hi></abbr><ex>ς</ex></expan> ος
                    <lb n="4"/><supplied reason="lost">μό</supplied>νον ἔγινε ἐκ
                    <lb n="5"/><supplied reason="lost">β</supplied>άθρ<hi rend="ligature">ου</hi> <expan><abbr>κ</abbr><ex>α</ex><abbr>τ</abbr><ex>ὰ</ex></expan> <hi rend="ligature">το</hi> <date from="1563-08-01" to="1568-08-31"><num value="7000">ˏζ</num><supplied reason="lost">ο</supplied><gap reason="lost" extent="unknown" unit="character"/>
                    <lb n="6"/><supplied reason="lost">μη</supplied><hi rend="ligature">νὴ</hi> Αυγ<hi rend="ligature">ου</hi>στ<supplied reason="lost">ῳ</supplied></date><gap reason="lost" extent="unknown" unit="character"/>
                </ab>
            </div>
            <div type="apparatus">
                <p> line 5: Dimitris Liakos restores the second digit of the year as ρ=100, which would give a date after 1592 (=anno mundi 7100). This is incompatible with the known dates of the superiorship of the abbot Maximos referred to in the text (1563-1568). Therefore, the restoration proposed here is ο=70 (i.e., 707X), which generates a date ranging from 1562 to 1571. The third digit must have been α, β, γ, δ, ε, or ς (i.e., 7071-7076 = 1563-1568). In any case, it is clear that this was a three-digit number (with a place value of 0 hundreds).</p>
            </div>
